  "findings": {
    "key_accounting": "The 54 exact held keys are a subset of the original 571-key join; their OCHA disagreement is the sole discriminator between this group and the OCHA-concordant group after the recorded screen. The 54 remain held in the historical disposition and no acceptance/credit is asserted here.",
    "per_key_source_membership": "All 54 centers hit their original assigned GeoBoundaries source member: Moheli index 20155 / shapeID 22816118B12510721755829, Anjouan index 20156 / shapeID 22816118B92166148047088, Grande Comore index 20157 / shapeID 22816118B95538827312271.",
    "retained_source_coverage": "For each of the three source-target coverage bindings in source-004, every one of the 54 exact (x,y) cells appears with class mapped_land_support. The source-evidence body labels the 2019 OCHA geometry as non-operative comparator-only; it is not an adopted source/authority operand.",
    "retained_stock_native_diagnostic": "The original full-scope stock diagnostic requested 571 cells, reports 571 supported, 0 held, first_failure=null. Thus the diagnostic already screened these 54 as supported within the original 571-cell request; it did not consume OCHA as a negative or establish a constructor result/current ownership/acceptance.",
    "physical_and_adverse_context": "Within the prior GSHHG center-hit flag, 26/54 have mapped-land center hits and 28/54 do not. All 54 have zero inland-water hits and zero whole-target-difference center hits. Do not conflate the separate GSHHG center-hit comparator flag with source-004 mapped_land_support, and do not erase the adverse OCHA comparison.",
    "official_primary_law": "The Comoros Ministry of Justice-hosted Law 11-006/AU (2 May 2011) states that territorial administration is provided by communes, autonomous islands and State decentralized services (Art. 1); Article 7 organizes prefectures under Mwali/Mohéli, Ngazidja/Grande Comore and Ndzuwani/Anjouan; Articles 8–11 define communes and their village groupings. This corroborates the island-level administrative identities used by the three original source features. It does not give GIS coordinates, certify exact raster centers against legal boundaries, or establish contemporary 2026 borders.",
    "census_source": "INSEED 2017 RGPH catalog describes ZD as its lowest geographic level and its enumerator manual states ZD maps define the zone limits. The catalog materials inspected list PDFs, not downloadable boundary vectors or a key-to-ZD assignment for these 54; no such assignment is asserted.",
    "competitor_context": "Previously retained v4 records cover the registered catalogue, exact 571 source vectors, complete FRA ADM1/2/3 pair matrices (1,287 pairs, 0 intersections), and dated disjoint IGN Mayotte context. These are bounded context, not an exhaustive universe of unregistered sources. OCHA remains non-operative; its geometry is not redistributed and its asserted license was not verified.",
    "decision": "The OCHA discrepancy alone is not a frozen-contract negative predicate because the original contract does not name OCHA as operative evidence. The exact source membership, all three source-evidence land-support bindings, zero inland-water/whole-target-difference hits, and 571/571 supported stock diagnostic provide a concrete basis to attempt the normal additive constructor for this exact 54-key subset. This checkpoint does not claim constructor qualification, current effective owner zero, selected-state conservation, acceptance or credit. Keep 54 held/pending until a distinct 54-key constructor and required review are completed."
  },
  "next_reasonable_step": "From a separately owned, exact 54-only proposal/authority input, run the existing stock native constructor once against the retained source-004 and full 571 diagnostic evidence, keeping the 485 accepted keys and 32 proposal disjoint. If constructor output is supported, reconcile selected-native conservation and obtain the existing independent reviewer; otherwise retain its exact failed predicates. Do not modify PR2739.",
